<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rio Grande do Sul</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-grande">Rio Grande</a> do Sul is the southernmost province, now a state, of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, bordering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruguay">Uruguay</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a>. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a> it was the scene of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ragamuffin-war">Farroupilha</a> or Ragamuffin War of 1835–1845, in which republican separatists maintained an independent republic for nearly a decade. Accounts of the Brazilian Empire cite the conflict as one of the regional rebellions that tested the young empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rio-grande-do-sul.jpg" alt="Rio Grande do Sul" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Srfortes · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bandeira_do_Rio_Grande_do_Sul.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
